---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { classes } from '../../../styles';
---
<DocsLayout title="Layout" description="Display, position, flow, media, and container utilities."><header><p class={classes.eyebrow}>Utility reference</p><h1 class={classes.title}>Layout</h1><p class={classes.lead}>Display, position, flow, media, and container utilities.</p></header><section class={classes.section}><h2 class={classes.heading}>Classes</h2><p class={classes.copy}>block, inline, inline-block, flex, inline-flex, grid, inline-grid, flow-root, contents, hidden, table display forms, sr-only, not-sr-only, static, fixed, absolute, relative, sticky, visible, invisible, z-*, inset-*, top/right/bottom/left-*, overflow-*, overscroll-*, aspect-*, object-*, columns-*, break-*, float-*, clear-*, box-*, and container.</p></section><section class={classes.section}><h2 class={classes.heading}>Containment</h2><pre class={classes.code}><code>content-visibility-auto contain-[layout_paint]{`\n`}contain-intrinsic-size-[auto_800px] contain-intrinsic-inline-size-4</code></pre><p class={classes.copy}>Use content-visibility-visible, content-visibility-auto, or content-visibility-hidden. Containment supports none, content, strict, size, inline-size, layout, style, paint, and static bracket values. Intrinsic size utilities accept spacing numbers, bracket values, and custom properties.</p></section></DocsLayout>
